// The plan tools/deck/scale.mjs scaled the prologue's deck by (stage 6, 2026-11-21; docs/story/deck/scale.md says why):
//   git show 65a7b84:data/planets/prolog/prolog.deck > old.deck
//   node tools/deck/scale.mjs tools/deck/prolog-x2.plan old.deck data/planets/prolog/prolog.deck
// Stretches are at old coordinates (a cell boundary of the stage 5 deck); fills, markers, zones, props and cams after them
// are in the new deck's coordinates.

header
header Scaled 2x as a whole from the stage 5 deck (65a7b84) by tools/deck/scale.mjs with tools/deck/prolog-x2.plan, with
header extra way in five places (docs/story/deck/scale.md: why, the mapping of old points, the doors, rooms and the pod size).
header The Grunts' doors are 8 m, the Reapers' blast doors 12-16 m; the crawl ducts kept their 4 m cross-section.
header The 2 on the DECK line is that scale: the sim's size classes need twice their room (Deck.GapScale, NavGrid). Grate windows
header into a duct reach the duct's kept band.

factor 2

// Extra way (old x or y, new cells put in): the order of the sections and the story's beats stay as they were.
stretch x 49 16    // the Buchtengang R0 (bays to deck A) 16 m longer
stretch y 44 16    // the links WL, EL, the service passage S and duct V1a 16 m longer; the pod bay R16 16 m deeper
stretch y 70 16    // deck B (R6) 16 m deeper; the Notgang R15 16 m longer
stretch x 141 24   // the spine R10, the parallel corridors P1, P2, the cable corridor K and duct V2 24 m longer
stretch x 250 48   // the pod bay R16 48 m wider: three of the game's pods (47.5 m across) side by side

// 21 x 14 tiles of 30 m (prolog.psf), as the old 270 x 180 was 9 x 6.
pad 630 420

// Heights: twice the old, but the core chamber 2.5 times (it must feel huge) and the pod bay as tall as a pod (43.5 m) needs.
height R9 40
height R16 56

// The core chamber R9 (160-224 x 232-296, the core at 192,264, 8 m round) gets cover for a fight that is played:
// four pillars from floor to ceiling round the core, a console bank on the west and on the east wall (the east one beside
// the vent V the Locator crawls in by), two crate stacks in the side lanes and two by the door J. Every way round the core
// and through I, J, K and M stays 9 m wide or more, so the Reapers still get round (deck.mjs checks it).
fill # 172 240 176 244
fill # 208 240 212 244
fill # 172 284 176 288
fill # 208 284 212 288
fill c 160 258 166 262
fill c 218 274 224 278
fill c 168 270 171 273
fill c 213 254 216 257
fill c 178 282 181 285
fill c 203 282 206 285
marker console_r9_w 167.5 260 180 terminal
marker console_r9_e 216.5 276 0 terminal
// Loose crates near the chamber's doors for the barricades (the old pile in R8 stays): two by I, two by J, and two in the NE
// corner behind the east console bank (in front of M they shut the Reapers out of P2).
prop crate_r9_1 crate_large 176 236 0 305
prop crate_r9_2 crate_large 208 236 0 306
prop crate_r9_3 crate_large 176 291 0 307
prop crate_r9_4 crate_large 208 291 0 308
prop crate_r9_5 crate_large 218 284 90 309
prop crate_r9_6 crate_large 218 289 90 310

// The pod bay R16 (432-600 x 24-120, the Notgang's mouth R15a at 512-528 in the north wall, the catwalk at y 108-113):
// three of the game's pods at their own size, 52 m apart and 8 m from the walls; pod 3 (the one that launches) in the east.
marker pod_1 464 54 90
marker pod_2 516 54 90
marker pod_3 568 54 90
marker pod_3_hatch 568 74 270
zone pod_zone 544 64 592 96 trigger
// The Abwurf film's camera on the catwalk, looking down at pod 3 (its old place was beside a 7 m pod).
cam cam_abwurf_1 520 110 48 311 -25
